    build/bin/clang -o whatever whatever.c -O2 -g

or:

    build/bin/clang++ -o whatever whatever.cpp -O2 -g

Take a look at pizfix/stdfil-include/stdfil.h for Fil-C-specific APIs. You can
optionally #include <stdfil.h> if you find those APIs useful.

New releases are at: https://github.com/pizlonator/fil-c/releases
More information on the website: https://fil-c.org/

Have fun and thank you for trying filc-0.684-linux-x86_64.
